Quake @VERSION@ for AmigaOS 3.x (AmiCradle)
============================================

Quake by id Software (1996), from the Amiga Quake 2.30 sources by Frank
Wille and Steffen Haeuser, built with GCC for a 68040 or 68060 with an
FPU, on ACGame (AGA or RTG) with sound through AHI. Status: TESTING, not a
release.

Requirements
------------

- AmigaOS 3.x, a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU, AGA or an RTG board.
- 16 MB of free Fast RAM for the game (quake -mem N for another size).
- AHI for the sound.
- Quake's data: id1/pak0.pak, from the shareware version or your own
  copy of the full game (see id1/ReadMe.txt).

Installing
----------

Unpack the archive where you keep games (lha x quake-...lha Games:), then
copy pak0.pak (and pak1.pak of the full game) into the drawer's id1 drawer.

Playing
-------

- Double-click the quake icon, or from a Shell: cd to the drawer, then
  quake. The PC version's command line works (quake +timedemo demo1).
- ENV:ACGame/Display set to AGA or RTG chooses the screen.
- The PC version's keys; ` opens the console. The mouse turns; hold the
  mlook key (or bind +mlook) to look up and down.
- This build draws with Quake's C code, not the 2.30 release's 68k
  assembly, and has no CD audio and no network play yet.

Licence
-------

Quake's source is under the GNU General Public License, version 2
(COPYING.txt, id's own copy). The Amiga port is Frank Wille's and Steffen
Haeuser's (Aminet game/shoot/Quake_src); see amiga230/README.md in the
source for the files of that release this build leaves out. The game data
is id Software's and is not part of this archive.

